## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical PCA deployment in a streaming, real-world telemetry context with missing data and the need for interpretable components. It probes method selection, online updating, drift handling, and actionable alerting under latency constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Streaming PCA variants (IPCA, PPCA, Sparse PCA)
- Handling missing data online
- Component interpretability via sparsity and rotation
- Drift detection on loadings and actionable alerts
- Latency budgeting in edge-to-cloud pipelines

## Code Example
````javascript
// Pseudo: online update loop snippet
for (event of stream) {
  x = impute(event.features);
  x = scale(x);
  subspace = ipca.partial_fit(x);
  score = reconstruct_error(x, subspace);
  if (drift_detected(subspace.loadings)) alert();
}
````

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you tune drift thresholds for varying load conditions?
- How would you validate robustness to bursty missing data and concept drift?
